  "question": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> coal is burnt in a bomb calorimeter in excess of oxygen at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>298</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>atm</mi></math> pressure.</p><p>The temperature of the calorimeter rises from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>298</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>. The enthalpy change during the combustion of coal is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math>&nbsp;is_____(Given : Heat capacity of bomb calorimeter <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>kJK</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. Assume coal to be pure carbon)</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "200",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>;</mo><mi>&#916;H</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>xkJ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>mole</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>C&#916;T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi></math> heat is released for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Carbon</mi></math></p><p>For <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;mole &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Carbon</mi></math>&#39;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>40</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>12</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>400</mn><mn>24</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>mole</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#916;E</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#916;H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#8757;</mo><msub><mi>&#916;n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn></math></p></blockquote>",
